      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that `microdroid_kernel_signed_supports_uefi_boot` is not missing this property and ideally, we want the only diff between the 2 images to be `supports_uefi_boot`.\n\nIIUC the syntax, we should therefore set `props` this way:\n```\nprops: [\n    {\n            name: \"com.android.virt.cap\",\n            value: \"supports_uefi_boot\",\n    },\n],\nsoong_config_variables: {\n    release_avf_enable_llpvm_changes: {\n        props: [\n            {\n                name: \"com.android.virt.cap\",\n                value: \"secretkeeper_protection|supports_uefi_boot\",\n            },\n        ],\n    },\n},\n```\nSo that the `secretkeeper_protection` capability remains set when the `release_avf_enable_llpvm_changes` Android flag is enabled.\n\nSame for the `rollback_index` (which probably defaults to 0 otherwise).\n\nI _think_ you can [DRY](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don%27t_repeat_yourself) the \"`1`\" between the 2 images by defining a Soong variable\n```\nMICRODROID_ROLLBACK_INDEX \u003d 1\n```\nand using it in both targets:\n```\nrollback_index: MICRODROID_ROLLBACK_INDEX,\n```\nbut please let me know if that doesn\u0027t work.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 485,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 485,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "4eebad1b9fc5045640210967b1103ccb768b6f8f",
